  "2026-11-17T11:55:01.071Z",codex-sol,"Round AU: verified all four review threads against the current code and confirmed PR #295 remains open. Branch contains current main, so no merge commit is needed. Quoted fallback pins now refresh and restore in every hook rewrite, covering both quotes and space/equals spellings. Continuation checks the prepared heading against the current day in RELEASE_TIMEZONE before publication and again immediately before tagging. A mismatch fails with a re-prepare instruction because mutating the already protected commit and verified artifact would break the existing immutable handoff design. The decision step rejects a resumed plan with missing or empty heading_date even when installed dist is stale. Rebuilt tracked daily-release and release-continuation outputs, including declarations and maps. Five targeted behavior regressions pass; final full coverage and reference suites are running. Initial lint and test-cleanup duplication findings were corrected; thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-11-17T12:14:38.764Z",codex-sol,"AU verification update: the final five-file focused command passed 182/182 tests with zero skips or failures; the six selected behavior and attestation regressions also passed. Typecheck, lint, docstring (50 sources, 378 declarations), duplication (0 clones, 0%), release-date verification and changelog:check passed. Packed npm and native Bun acceptance both passed 192 SDK/caller/attestation cases, 12 CLI JSON/TOON checks, 64 handoff cases and 256 tamper refusals. The rewritten release-heading acceptance passed its complete release:check, including coverage: 1707 passed, 0 failed, 2 existing opt-in real-data skips, with 100% statements, branches, functions and lines across all 50 required sources. The direct coverage run measured the same 100% but failed the unchanged five-second regular-input child startup watchdog already tracked by ops-input-startup-timeout; isolated retry passed 6/6. A direct full coverage retry is now running without the other test runs. The inline quoted-date regex uses equivalent hexadecimal quote escapes because literal quotes confuse the existing attestation shell audit; its gate remains unchanged and passes."
