  "2026-11-17T15:45:43.703Z",codex-sol,"Round AX final results: npm run build, npm run build:test, npm run typecheck, npm run lint and npm run duplication passed (0% duplication). The four named targeted suites passed 174 tests with zero failures/skips. npm run coverage passed 1709 tests with zero failures and 2 optional real-data skips, measuring all 50 intended source files at 100% statements/branches/functions/lines with unchanged thresholds and scope. node test/release-heading-full-gate.acceptance.ts passed its real rewritten release:check, including another complete 100% coverage run, audits, pack dry run, changelog/date/section checks, attestation and lifecycle checks. Every referencing unit-test file ran through the full suite; node test/continuation-selection.acceptance.ts passed both real packed npm and native Bun consumers using the requested network timeout. Initial startup and install failures and the execution-context retries remain recorded above. ops-b2bs was retitled exactly as requested without changing its status or protected timestamps. Open limitations are tracked by ops-release-generator-timezone, ops-input-startup-timeout and ops-packed-network-options. The claim is released next; final tag fetch, generator-only changelog refresh/check and commit follow as the no-more-tracker-writes boundary. No item was closed, no review thread was changed, and nothing was published."
  "2026-11-17T16:21:38.509Z",codex-sol,"Round AZ verified both findings before changes. PR #295 remains open and the branch contains origin/main. The pinned pm-changelog 2026.11.6 reads git log -1 --format=%cI (node_modules/pm-changelog/dist/release-context.js:496), uses that timestamp for the heading (line 153), and retains its literal date prefix (lines 554-558). The heading adapter now mirrors it without RELEASE_TIMEZONE conversion. The publication-only refusal and advisory check after npm acceptance remain unchanged. A red-first regression reproduced the old offset mismatch; the corrected test compares the real tagged generator for UTC and +01:00 representations of the same instant. A shared snapshot helper removes staged and unstaged source deletions before copying existing tracked files; its regression also checks edited files and staged additions. npm run build and npm run build:test passed; no tracked dist bytes changed because the changed workflow adapter is executed directly and excluded from the root build."
